>>care of all of them somehow.
> 
> They turn to flesh and become real skeletons or acid blobs.  The problem
> is that the statue of the stone golum is turning to stone and becoming a
> real stone golem.  It should be turning to flesh and becoming a real
> flesh golem.

If your premise is: Everything has to go to flesh, then yes (if you take
'stone to flesh' literally). I guess the programm sets the premise:
Everything has to go back to his *living (or better: moving) origin*, and
in this case a stone golem seems right on a first glance.

There still seems some strange behavior with transforming golems: Recently
I touched a leather golem while polymorphed into a cockatrice. The result
was an angry and very alive stone golem (not exactly what poor little
cockatrice expected). Since stone golems can't be stoned anymore and if
you take 'stone to flesh' zapped on a stone golem as an 'act of reverse
stoning', then Netbrian is (partially) right: The result could be *any
kind of a golem* (including flesh golem) but never a stone golem.

